Sentence 1: Ildjarn
Ildjarn Ildjarn was a black metal project from Norway that formed in 1991.
Sentence 2: Ildjarn recorded music until 1997 but did not officially end until 2005.
Sentence 3: The man behind Ildjarn was Vidar Vaaer, although some releases were collaborations with a musician known as Nidhogg.
Sentence 4: Ildjarn's music was a very simple and lo-fi brand of black metal, with most songs composed of basic drum patterns, a couple of riffs, and unintelligible vocals.
Sentence 5: Two Ildjarn albums were made entirely on a synthesizer.
