Sentence 1: North American Free Trade Agreement
North American Free Trade Agreement The North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA; Spanish: "Tratado de Libre Comercio de América del Norte", TLCAN; French: "Accord de libre-échange nord-américain", ALÉNA) is an agreement signed by Canada, Mexico, and the United States, creating a trilateral trade bloc in North America.
Sentence 2: The North American Free Trade Agreement (NAFTA) is an agreement between Canada, Mexico and the United States to eliminate tariffs on goods traded between themselves.
