Sentence 1: Unetice culture
Unetice culture The Únětice culture (, Czech Únětická kultura, German Aunjetitzer Kultur, Polish Kultura unietycka) is an archaeological culture at the start of the Central European Bronze Age, dated roughly to about 2300–1600BC.
Sentence 2: Today, the Únětice culture is known from about 1,400 sites in the Czech Republic and Slovakia, 550 sites in Poland, and, in Germany, about 500 sites and loose finds locations.
Sentence 3: The Únětice culture is also known from north-eastern Austria (in association with the so-called the Böheimkirchen Group),
