Sentence 1: Operation Primicia
Operation Primicia Operación Primicia (, "Operation Scoop") was a large guerrilla attack that took place on 5 October 1975, in Formosa, Argentina.
Sentence 2: Operativo Independencia
Operativo Independencia Operativo Independencia (Spanish for "Operation Independence") was the code-name of the Argentine military operation in the Tucumán Province, started in 1975 to crush the ERP —"Ejército Revolucionario del Pueblo" or "People's Revolutionary Army"—, a Guevarist guerrilla group, which tried to create a Vietnam-style war front in the Tucumán Province, in northwestern Argentina.
Sentence 3: Operation Condor
Operation Condor Operation Condor (, also known as "Plan Cóndor"; ) was a United States–backed campaign of political repression and state terror involving intelligence operations and assassination of opponents, officially implemented in 1975 by the right-wing dictatorships of the Southern Cone of South America.
