Sentence 3: Biker metal Biker metal (also known as biker punk) is a fusion genre that combines elements of punk rock, heavy metal, rock and roll and blues, that was pioneered in the late-1970s to early-1980s in England and the United States, by Motörhead, Plasmatics, Anti-Nowhere League and Girlschool.
Sentence 4: Biker metal has been described as being influenced by punk rock, rock and roll, heavy metal and blues.
