Sentence 1: Connaraceae
Connaraceae Connaraceae is a pan-tropical plant family of 19 genera and more than 180 species of largely evergreen trees, woody shrubs and climbers.
Sentence 2: Connaraceae is a tropical family, the most important genera of which, "Connarus" (approximately 80 species) and "Rourea" (40-70 species) have a pan-tropical distribution.. Their habitat is generally lowland tropical rain forest and savanna.
Sentence 3: Connaraceae are typically evergreen trees, shrubs or climbers.
Sentence 4: "Connarus" is represented by species in all three lifeforms, while "Rourea" species are climbers.
