Sentence 2: Battle of Leyte
Battle of Leyte The Battle of Leyte (Filipino: "Labanan sa Leyte", Waray: "Gubat ha Leyte", 17 October – 26 December 1944) in the Pacific campaign of World War II was the amphibious invasion of the island of Leyte in the Philippines by American forces and Filipino guerrillas under the command of General Douglas MacArthur, who fought against the Imperial Japanese Army in the Philippines led by General Tomoyuki Yamashita.
