Sentence 1: Olde English Bulldogge
Olde English Bulldogge The Old English Bulldog is an American dog breed.
Sentence 2: In the 1970s David Leavitt created a true-breeding lineage as a re-creation of the healthier working bulldog from early nineteenth century England.
Sentence 3: Using a breeding scheme developed for cattle, Leavitt crossed English bulldogs, American Bulldogs, Bull Mastiffs and American Pit Bull Terriers.
Sentence 4: The result was an athletic breed that looks similar to the bulldogs of 1820, but also has a friendly temperament with less health issues.
Sentence 5: Pure breed Olde English Bulldogges can be registered under the "International Olde English Bulldogge Association" and other respected Associations.
