Sentence 1: Afroasiatic languages
Afroasiatic languages Afroasiatic (Afro-Asiatic), also known as Afrasian and in older sources as Hamito-Semitic (Chamito-Semitic) or Semito-Hamitic, is a large language family of about 300 languages.
Sentence 2: The phylum has six branches: Berber, Chadic, Cushitic, Egyptian, Omotic and Semitic.
Sentence 3: Most people in the country speak Afroasiatic languages of the Cushitic or Semitic branches.
Sentence 4: They speak Amharic, an Afro-Asiatic language of the Semitic branch, a member of the Ethiosemitic group, which serves as the official language of Ethiopia.
