Sentence 1: Betawi people
Betawi people Betawi people or Betawis (Orang Betawi in Indonesian, meaning "people of Batavia") are an Austronesian ethnic group native to the city of Jakarta and its immediate outskirts, as such often described as the native inhabitants of the city.
Sentence 2: They are the descendants of the people who inhabited Batavia (the colonial name of Jakarta) from the 17th century onwards.
Sentence 3: Among the Betawi ethnic Christians, some have claimed that they are the descendants of the Portuguese Mardijker which intermarried with the local population, who mainly settled in the area of Kampung Tugu, North Jakarta.
