Kumaon Mastiff The Kumaon Mastiff (Kumauni: सिप्रो कुकुर), also known as the Indian Mastiff and Bulli, is a rare Molosser-type working breed of dog originating in Uttarakhand state of India.
Sentence 2: Originally bred as a watch dog and livestock guardian in the hills of Kumaon, this dog is rare even in the region of its origin.
Sentence 3: It is said that the dogs primitive ancestors were domiciled in the Kumaon region.
Sentence 4: Kumaon Mastiff is a large dog with fairly lean, muscular, well-boned bodies.
