Sentence 1: Operation Ten-Go
Operation Ten-Go In April 1945, the (the largest battleship in the world), along with nine other Japanese warships, embarked from Japan on a deliberate suicide attack upon Allied forces engaged in the Battle of Okinawa.
Sentence 2: The Japanese force was attacked, stopped, and almost destroyed by United States carrier-borne aircraft before reaching Okinawa.
Sentence 3: "Yamato" and five other Japanese warships were sunk.
Sentence 4: The battle also exhibited Japan's willingness to sacrifice entire ships, even the
Sentence 5: About 100 of the Japanese aircraft were lost in the attack.
Sentence 6: "Ten-Go" was the last major Japanese naval operation of the war, and the remaining Japanese warships had little involvement in combat operations for the rest of the conflict.
Sentence 7: Battle of Okinawa
