Sentence 1: Gymnosphaerid
Gymnosphaerid The gymnosphaerids (or Gymnosphaerida) are a small group of heliozoan protists found in marine environments.
Sentence 2: There are only three genera, each with a single species: "Gymnosphaera albida", "Hedraiophrys hovassei", and "Actinocoryne contractilis".
Sentence 3: Gymnosphaerids were originally considered centrohelids, which also have microtubules in a triangular-hexagonal array, but are set apart from the others by the structure of the central granule and the mitochondria, which have tubular cristae.
Sentence 4: Ichneumonoidea
